droidcam (2.1.7-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/patches/0001-wait-for-the-first-picture-and-say-why-the-stream-ends.patch: the client waits for the phone's first picture, receives whole or fails,
    and says why a stream ends.
    The DroidCam app (6.28, Android 10) answers the request at once and opens the phone's camera afterwards: the first frame came 7 to 18 seconds later,
    and the client's receive timeout (5 seconds and the microseconds select() leaves in the same timeval, about 6) ended its video thread in silence with
    nothing written to the video device; the same phone then sent frames in bursts with gaps of 5 seconds and more, which that timeout would also take for
    the end of the stream. The first frame is now waited for up to 60 seconds (it says so after two), a running stream is given 15 seconds between frames,
    a stream that sends no picture or is lost is said, and droidcam-cli exits with 3 or 4 (1 for the earlier failures) where it used to stay running; the
    window program (droidcam) does what its Stop button does and shows Connect again.
  * A receive that a signal interrupts while the program runs goes on (Ctrl+Z and fg: SIGCONT interrupts a receive with a timeout, signal(7)); it used to end
    the stream in silence. The video header, the frame length and the frame are received whole or the receive fails (recv with MSG_WAITALL returned fewer bytes
    after a timeout in the middle of a frame, which left the stream out of step), and a frame length of 0 or above the frame buffer ends the stream.
  * -size is not applied when the loopback device keeps its first size: the client says which size it stays at. When the phone sends another size than the
    device takes, the client says so once ("the phone sends WxH, shown at WxH").
  * No upstream commit, issue or pull request covers it (dev47apps/droidcam-linux-client searched on 2026-11-24: no commit after v2.1.7; issues #180 and #94,
    closed, were Ctrl+C that did nothing).
  * tests/first-frame: a stand-in for the app (server.py, with the header and framing recorded from the phone), a V4L2 shim, cases.sh (red on 2.1.7-1 and green
    on this version, without a phone) and gui-cases.sh (the window program in a container with a virtual display).
  * The Depends are unchanged: the client already decodes the app's JPEG frames with libturbojpeg (Build-Depends libturbojpeg0-dev, shlibs adds the runtime package); no decoder was missing.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:00:56 +0000

droidcam (2.1.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Upstream release 2.1.7 of Dev47Apps' Linux client for DroidCam (tag v2.1.7, commit c8a0cc97663d), built from the release tag's source.
    The client and the command line client are built as upstream's Makefile builds them; the bundled v4l2loopback-dc kernel module and the
    install scripts are not used, because the edition uses Debian's v4l2loopback-dkms (the client opens any v4l2loopback device).
  * The desktop entry and the icon are the package's own (upstream's entry names /opt paths).
  * Not in Debian (no source package ever, no wnpp bug open); carried by the edition (missing-from-debian-ask-why).

